  "body": "### What is the issue with the Cookie Store API Standard?\n\nThere should be an option to set cookies without a `Secure` attribute.\n\nSetting aside the question of intentionally handicapping a standard API, I don't think the API should assume that a website running in a secure context is able to set a secure cookie. Secure contexts and the `Secure` cookie attributes are defined by 2 different specifications that don't have any overlap. And the specification for the cookie attribute leaves the exact behavior up to each user agent.\n\nFor example, Safari treats `http://localhost` as a secure context but not as a secure channel for cookies.\n\nAs long as the `Secure` attribute is set by default, I still think the API will \"encourage better decisions around security.\"",
